  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{arccotx}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
